modern_usage.modern_context:
In modern times, the ancient Hindu name 'Amaranth' has gained popularity due to its health benefits and versatility. Amaranth is a gluten-free pseudo-cereal that is rich in protein, fiber, iron, and other essential vitamins and minerals. It is often used in the vegan and health food communities as a nutritious alternative to grains and is becoming increasingly popular in alternative medicine practices due to its anti-inflammatory properties.

Three platforms where Amaranth is commonly seen are Instagram, where its vibrant color and unique presentation make for visually appealing posts;
Whole Foods Market, where it is sold in various forms such as flour, cooked grains, and puffs;
And Amazon, where it can be easily purchased in bulk for home cooking and baking.
